exp-21b: send the three format-list predicates back to being static.

The tail of exp-21, applied after it.  Once tu_image_init() asks
tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear() instead of comparing the three
predicates itself, tu6_format_list_has_swaps(),
tu6_format_list_reinterprets_r8g8_r16() and
tu6_format_list_swaps_are_uniform() have no caller outside tu_formats.cc: 0004
exported the first two (they were static in tu_image.cc before it), 0005
exported the third, and this removes the exports again - 4 hunks +16/-18, no
behaviour change.

Kept in its own file because of whose hunks it lands on.  The definitions
belong to three patches: has_swaps() and reinterprets_r8g8_r16() are 0004's,
and swaps_are_uniform() is 0005's, rewritten by 0010 - so putting "static"
above them and deleting the declarations touches 0004, 0005 and 0010, whose
own hunks are the ones that introduced those lines.  That is a second,
separate gate, and it is not worth settling in the same run as the equivalence
check of exp-21: if the counters move, the tail should not be in the way.

NOT BUILT, NOT MEASURED.  Apply after experiments/exp-21-mutable-one-
decision.patch, revert first.

